From 72c94c382c3db8f75aa89f33becb6b181b18b306 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:41:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add LICENSE matching setuptools' default license_files glob

setuptools only auto-discovers license files at the project root that
match LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS*. The project's own BSD, GPL
and LGPL license texts are named without any of those prefixes, so
despite the project declaring "License: BSD" and COPYING pointing to
these three files, none of the actual license text ships in the wheel's
dist-info/licenses/ -- only COPYING and AUTHORS do.

Add a LICENSE file duplicating BSD's text (the license this package
declares itself under) so it is picked up by the default glob with no
setup.cfg/setup.py change, mirroring how MeCab (also BSD/GPL/LGPL
tri-licensed) resolves the same gap upstream.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [blocked: this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 LICENSE | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE

diff --git a/LICENSE b/LICENSE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d8fe0ef
--- /dev/null
